 Innovative optics and computer simulations describe the wave dynamics in detail
A team of researchers at the Max Planck Institute for Dynamics and Self-Organization (MPI-DS) and the Leibniz University Hannover has developed a new method that allows them to study the behavior of waves around a stone pier in unprecedented detail. By combining innovative optics and advanced computer simulations, they were able to measure and calculate the dynamics of the waves in real-time.
Waves around a pier can be much higher than expected due to the "shadowing effect" of the pier. In this study, the researchers focused on the area directly behind the pier, where waves tend to accumulate.
